spec ri02-edge-into-deleted-node-lpg: 2 sessions, 6 permutations
# RI02. Both transactions open before either writes: s1 DETACH DELETEs b, s2 creates
# an edge into b. Whichever writes second is refused while the first is open and after
# it commits; no permutation leaves an edge to a dead node.
# Through the lpg API.
# The final dangling probe must count 0 in every permutation: an edge to a dead node
# is never committed (catalogue §9 point 3).

starting permutation: s1d s1c s2e s2c
step s1d: lpg: detach-delete b (RemoveEdge of each in-arc, RemoveAllEdgesFrom, RemoveNode)
step s1c: lpg: Session.EndVersionedTx
step s2e: lpg: AddEdge(a, b)
ERROR: serialization conflict
step s2c: lpg: Session.EndVersionedTx
ERROR: serialization conflict
final final: MATCH (n) RETURN n.name AS name ORDER BY name
name
----
"a" 
(1 row)
final edges: MATCH (x)-[r]->(y) RETURN x.name AS src, r.id AS id, y.name AS dst ORDER BY src, id, dst
src|id|dst
---+--+---
(0 rows)
final dangling: <lpg: arcs touching a dead node, at a fresh snapshot>
live_arcs|dangling
---------+--------
0        |0       
(1 row)

